{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1767 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "9269bb721b1d01b0ac4fdbf32b03b3b2fe3e46f458b3a0e5f2514912d565e4cb" :edb/db-before-t 1766 :edb/db-after-t 1767 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535079 50 #inst "2026-10-08T16:23:27.540Z" 13194139535079 true] [17592186184291 1020 #edb/ref 17592186330116 13194139535079 true] [17592186184292 1020 #edb/ref 17592186330113 13194139535079 true] [17592186184292 1020 #edb/ref 17592186330123 13194139535079 true] [17592186330113 1017 #edb/ref 17592186330114 13194139535079 true] [17592186330113 1089 "q-347637" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330113 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535079 true] [17592186330113 1100 "Use the first two non-zero terms of the Taylor expansion of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ about $x=\\pi $ to approximate the value of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\pi +0.2).$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\pi +0.2)≈$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330113 1113 #uuid "9070d2fc-ef35-5217-a380-97c0b5a05359" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330113 1145 "We use Taylor's formula in the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+⋯,\n$$\n\nwith $f(x)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ and $a=\\pi .$ \n\nCalculating the necessary derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x \\\\ f(\\pi ) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\pi )=-1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{′}(\\pi ) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\pi )\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\pi )=0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{tan}^{2}⁡x+{sec}^{3}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{″}(\\pi ) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\pi ){tan}^{2}⁡(\\pi )+{sec}^{3}⁡(\\pi )=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Taylor series is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x & =-1+(0)(x-\\pi )+\\frac{(-1)}{2!}(x-\\pi )^{2}+⋯ \\\\  & =-1-\\frac{1}{2}(x-\\pi )^{2}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute $x=\\pi +0.2$ into the above to approximate $\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\pi +0.2).$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\pi +0.2) & ≈-1-\\frac{1}{2}{(\\pi +0.2-\\pi )}^{2} \\\\  & =-1-\\frac{1}{2}(0.2)^{2} \\\\  & =-1-\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{25}) \\\\  & =-1-\\frac{1}{50} \\\\  & =-\\frac{51}{50}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330114 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330115 13194139535079 true] [17592186330114 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535079 true] [17592186330114 1041 "field-1" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330114 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330115 13194139535079 true] [17592186330114 1110 #uuid "dae3ef6e-ab2e-5ade-ad19-cd3a59e37fff" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330115 1034 "-1.02" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330115 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535079 true] [17592186330115 1111 #uuid "aa61e374-3a73-5b17-9eb5-3eae45f312c9" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330116 1017 #edb/ref 17592186330117 13194139535079 true] [17592186330116 1017 #edb/ref 17592186330119 13194139535079 true] [17592186330116 1017 #edb/ref 17592186330121 13194139535079 true] [17592186330116 1089 "q-353859" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330116 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535079 true] [17592186330116 1100 "Find the first three non-zero terms of the Taylor expansion of $x{e}^{x+2}$ about $x=-1.$\n\n$x{e}^{x+2}=$ {{field-1}} $+\\,$\n{{field-2}}\n$(x+1)^{2}\\,+\\,$\n{{field-3}}\n$(x+1)^{3}+⋯$" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330116 1113 #uuid "ab2ebb5a-5574-563b-a19e-a919adb7c6dc" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330116 1145 "We use Taylor's theorem in the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(a)}{3!}(x-a)^{3}+⋯,\n$$\n\nwith $f(x)=x{e}^{x+2}$ and $a=-1.$ \n\nComputing the required derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =x{e}^{x+2} \\\\ f(-1) & =(-1){e}^{1}=-e \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & ={e}^{x+2}+x{e}^{x+2}=(1+x){e}^{x+2} \\\\ {f}^{′}(-1) & =(1-1){e}^{1}=0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & ={e}^{x+2}+(1+x){e}^{x+2}=(2+x){e}^{x+2} \\\\ {f}^{″}(-1) & =(2-1){e}^{1}=e \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & ={e}^{x+2}+(2+x){e}^{x+2}=(3+x){e}^{x+2} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(-1) & =(3-1){e}^{1}=2e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{x+2} & =-e+(0)(x+1)+\\frac{e}{2!}(x+1)^{2}+\\frac{2e}{3!}(x+1)^{3}⋯ \\\\  & =-e+\\frac{e}{2}(x+1)^{2}+\\frac{e}{3}(x+1)^{3}⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330117 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330118 13194139535079 true] [17592186330117 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535079 true] [17592186330117 1041 "field-1" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330117 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330118 13194139535079 true] [17592186330117 1110 #uuid "c2db4285-6cd5-5770-a25e-7d88e563f7f0" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330118 1034 "-e" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330118 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535079 true] [17592186330118 1111 #uuid "a09b2459-e7e0-5b55-a80a-e3ec777a3b87" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330119 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330120 13194139535079 true] [17592186330119 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535079 true] [17592186330119 1041 "field-2" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330119 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330120 13194139535079 true] [17592186330119 1110 #uuid "8f8808fb-ebd6-5821-8758-222afaa6e475" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330120 1034 "\\frac{e}{2}" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330120 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535079 true] [17592186330120 1111 #uuid "7ffbebfb-f837-5e6c-b95e-3d4c9ef7df85" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330121 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330122 13194139535079 true] [17592186330121 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535079 true] [17592186330121 1041 "field-3" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330121 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330122 13194139535079 true] [17592186330121 1110 #uuid "ecd3f18b-8e59-5ad0-bab0-fc4fce9c9fee" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330122 1034 "\\frac{e}{3}" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330122 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535079 true] [17592186330122 1111 #uuid "b4289a5e-3f0c-59c8-b77d-091d5a143d3f" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330123 1017 #edb/ref 17592186330124 13194139535079 true] [17592186330123 1089 "q-9623" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330123 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535079 true] [17592186330123 1100 "Use the first three non-zero terms of the Taylor expansion of $\\sqrt{x}$ about $x=4$ to approximate the value of $\\sqrt{\\pi }.$ Give your answer to $4$ decimal places." 13194139535079 true] [17592186330123 1113 #uuid "43923f1d-dfe1-5ab3-936a-6fc1d8791c67" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330123 1145 "We use Taylor's formula in the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+⋯,\n$$\n\nwith $a=4.$ \n\nCalculating the necessary derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\sqrt{x}={x}^{1/2} \\\\ f(4) & ={4}^{1/2}=2 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2} \\\\ {f}^{′}(4) & =\\frac{1}{2}(4)^{-1/2}=\\frac{1}{{2}^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2}){x}^{-3/2}=-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{-3/2} \\\\ {f}^{″}(4) & =-\\frac{1}{4}(4)^{-3/2}=-\\frac{1}{{2}^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Taylor series is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{x} & =2+\\frac{1}{{2}^{2}}(x-4)-\\frac{1}{2!}(\\frac{1}{{2}^{5}})(x-4)^{2}+⋯ \\\\  & =2+\\frac{x-4}{4}-\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{64}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute $x=\\pi $ into the above to approximate $\\sqrt{\\pi }.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\pi } & ≈2+\\frac{\\pi -4}{4}-\\frac{(\\pi -4)^{2}}{64} \\\\  & =1.773\\,9\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto $4$ decimal places." 13194139535079 true] [17592186330124 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330125 13194139535079 true] [17592186330124 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330126 13194139535079 true] [17592186330124 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330127 13194139535079 true] [17592186330124 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330128 13194139535079 true] [17592186330124 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330129 13194139535079 true] [17592186330124 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535079 true] [17592186330124 1041 "selection" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330124 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330129 13194139535079 true] [17592186330124 1110 #uuid "f7cd1b69-97b5-50fb-bf77-12efcb36b6cc" 13194139535079 true] [17592186330125 1034 "\\sqrt{\\pi }≈1.792\\,7" 13194139535079